  message: "Part 1 shipped in PR #1928: the io_primitives loader (IoBoundaryCatalog._from_dict, so shipped catalogues and every overlay) refuses an unknown key at top level, in a boundary row, a stdlib_other row and a completeness entry, naming it with a near-miss hint, via yaml_catalogs.reject_unknown_keys (lifted from taint's WI-rinaz helper, which now calls it). Live case found: docs/templates/bash-io-primitives.template.yaml's fs_delete: section (rm, shred) loaded zero rows; now fs_write. Accepted as human-read: seeded_from (init-catalogs stamp) and a completeness entry's source_url. Remaining: function_summaries, library_signatures, frameworks, dataflow_patterns loaders and their accepted-but-unread keys."  # b354
