  message: "Done across PR #1927 (io_primitives, dev d0061769ad) and PR #1929 (dev 479300f972): every catalogue loader -- taint (WI-rinaz), io_primitives, frameworks, library_signatures, function_summaries, dataflow_patterns -- refuses a key nothing reads through yaml_catalogs.reject_unknown_keys, naming file, level and key with a near-miss hint. Behavioral evidence: an overlay with net_sendd: / function: (the census repro) now fails 'unknown top-level key(s) net_sendd ... Did you mean: net_send' (CatalogueError, exit 2) instead of loading 0 rows; test_io_catalogue_unknown_keys.py / test_catalogue_unknown_keys.py exercise each loader and level through the real loaders. Accepted-but-unread keys deleted: frameworks linkers: (101 files) and detect: (3), library_signatures module_completeness: partial (5), DataflowConfig.calls. Dead rules deleted with notes: Graphene name_pattern, zio usage_call x2 -- the gaps they hid filed as WI-sorop. Live cases the strictness caught: the shipped bash template's fs_delete: (rm/shred now fs_write) and a test's in-house framework fixture that loaded zero patterns. Not done (outside the item text): function-summary VALUES no consumer reads (census K7), dataflow row values the maps ignore (K13)."  # e612
